{"parentUuid":"8b342966-fd44-4389-b974-2df7bdb43bde","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"52c38054-a209-4b88-9a0d-d98ba15865dd","version":"2.1.3","gitBranch":"main","slug":"vectorized-weaving-quail","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qo25z9ZwTTchiof9n24eJm","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenCode Plugin System Documentation\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nOpenCode plugins extend functionality by hooking into various events. A plugin is \"a **JavaScript/TypeScript module** that exports one or more plugin functions. Each function receives a context object and returns a hooks object.\"\n\n## Plugin Definition Structure\n\nPlugins follow this pattern:\n\n```javascript\nexport const MyPlugin = async ({ project, client, $, directory, worktree }) => {\n  return {\n    // Hook implementations\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Context parameters provided:**\n- `project`: Current project information\n- `directory`: Working directory\n- `worktree`: Git worktree path\n- `client`: OpenCode SDK client for AI interaction\n- `$`: Bun's shell API for command execution\n\n## Loading Mechanisms\n\n**Two installation approaches:**\n\n1. **Local files** - Place in `.opencode/plugin/` (project) or `~/.config/opencode/plugin/` (global)\n2. **NPM packages** - Specify in config via `opencode.json`\n\nBoth regular and scoped packages work. Packages auto-install using Bun with caching in `~/.cache/opencode/node_modules/`.\n\n## Available Hooks/Events\n\nPlugins subscribe to numerous event types:\n\n- **Commands**: `command.executed`\n- **Files**: `file.edited`, `file.watcher.updated`\n- **Installation**: `installation.updated`\n- **LSP**: `lsp.client.diagnostics`, `lsp.updated`\n- **Messages**: `message.part.removed`, `message.updated`, `message.removed`\n- **Permissions**: `permission.replied`, `permission.updated`\n- **Sessions**: `session.created`, `session.compacted`, `session.deleted`, `session.idle`, `session.status`, `session.updated`\n- **Tools**: `tool.execute.before`, `tool.execute.after`\n- **TUI**: `tui.prompt.append`, `tui.command.execute`, `tui.toast.show`\n\n## Plugin Lifecycle\n\nLoad order ensures predictable initialization:\n\n1. Global config\n2. Project config\n3. Global plugin directory\n4. Project plugin directory\n\nDuplicate npm packages load once; local and npm plugins with similar names load separately.\n\n## Dependencies Management\n\nAdd `package.json` to `.opencode/` directory specifying npm dependencies. OpenCode runs `bun install` automatically.\n\n## TypeScript Support\n\nPlugins can import types:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { Plugin } from \"@opencode-ai/plugin\"\n```\n\n## Specialized Capabilities\n\n**Custom Tools**: Plugins define domain-specific tools using schema and execution functions\n\n**Compaction Hooks**: `experimental.session.compacting` injects context before session summarization or replaces the compaction prompt entirely\n\n**Structured Logging**: Use `client.app.log()` with service, level, message, and extra fields (debug, info, warn, error levels)"}]},"uuid":"cda6de3e-fdf3-4376-afb9-142be8b02b2c","timestamp":"2026-01-10T10:47:29.303Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":92596,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# OpenCode Plugin System Documentation\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nOpenCode plugins extend functionality by hooking into various events. A plugin is \"a **JavaScript/TypeScript module** that exports one or more plugin functions. Each function receives a context object and returns a hooks object.\"\n\n## Plugin Definition Structure\n\nPlugins follow this pattern:\n\n```javascript\nexport const MyPlugin = async ({ project, client, $, directory, worktree }) => {\n  return {\n    // Hook implementations\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Context parameters provided:**\n- `project`: Current project information\n- `directory`: Working directory\n- `worktree`: Git worktree path\n- `client`: OpenCode SDK client for AI interaction\n- `$`: Bun'