{"parentUuid":"0b737466-40e5-45f4-a749-ec01162bdf2b","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"52c38054-a209-4b88-9a0d-d98ba15865dd","version":"2.1.3","gitBranch":"main","slug":"vectorized-weaving-quail","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01DaoCYQ2Cu3nJiTNxqQS6cu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019r439E9UQr3MuzcMRmFtyF","name":"TodoWrite","input":{"todos":[{"content":"Review OpenCode plugin documentation and architecture","status":"completed","activeForm":"Reviewing OpenCode plugin documentation and architecture"},{"content":"Analyze OpenCode event system and plugin implementation","status":"completed","activeForm":"Analyzing OpenCode event system and plugin implementation"},{"content":"Review Entire CLI hook system and strategy architecture","status":"completed","activeForm":"Reviewing Entire CLI hook system and strategy architecture"},{"content":"Identify integration points between OpenCode plugins and Entire hooks","status":"completed","activeForm":"Identifying integration points between OpenCode plugins and Entire hooks"},{"content":"Write findings document analyzing both systems","status":"completed","activeForm":"Writing findings document analyzing both systems"},{"content":"Write integration plan proposing implementation approach","status":"in_progress","activeForm":"Writing integration plan proposing implementation approach"}]}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68002,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":68002,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CWycv1KztHK9VTfQqFFoE","type":"assistant","uuid":"486d77ad-682f-4eca-a25c-80c218f80234","timestamp":"2026-01-10T11:29:36.771Z"}
{"parentUuid":"486d77ad-682f-4eca-a25c-80c218f80234","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"52c38054-a209-4b88-9a0d-d98ba15865dd","version":"2.1.3","gitBranch":"main","slug":"vectorized-weaving-quail","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01DaoCYQ2Cu3nJiTNxqQS6cu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X8Hju4V2egXKQQPbsr6o7n","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/docs/opencode-integration-plan.md","content":"# OpenCode Integration: Implementation Plan\n\n**Date:** 2026-01-10\n**Author:** Claude (Sonnet 4.5)\n**Status:** Proposal\n**Approach:** OpenCode Plugin (Option 1 from Findings)\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document outlines a concrete implementation plan for integrating OpenCode with the Entire CLI via an OpenCode plugin. The plugin will:\n\n1. Subscribe to OpenCode events\n2. Translate events to Entire CLI hook calls\n3. Export session data for checkpoint metadata\n4. Handle error cases and logging\n\n---\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        OpenCode CLI                          │\n│  ┌────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐   │\n│  │ Event Bus  │  │ Session Mgmt │  │ Tool Execution   │   │\n│  └─────┬──────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └─────┬────────────┘   │\n│        │                 │                 │                 │\n│        └─────────────────┴─────────────────┘                │\n│                          │                                   │\n│                          ▼                                   │\n│            ┌──────────────────────────┐                     │\n│            │ Entire Integration Plugin│                     │\n│            │  (opencode-entire)       │                     │\n│            └─────────────┬────────────┘                     │\n└──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n                           │ spawns commands\n                           │ with JSON input\n                           ▼\n              ┌─────────────────────────┐\n              │   Entire CLI Process    │\n              │  (entire hooks opencode)│\n              └────────────┬────────────┘\n                           │\n                           │ reads JSON from stdin\n                           │ performs git operations\n                           │ writes to .entire/\n                           ▼\n              ┌─────────────────────────┐\n              │   Git Repository        │\n              │  - Shadow branches      │\n              │  - Metadata branch      │\n              │  - Session state files  │\n              └─────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (MVP)\n\n**Goal:** Basic session tracking with checkpoint creation\n\n**Components:**\n\n1. **Entire CLI: OpenCode Hook Commands**\n   - Add `entire hooks opencode` subcommand group\n   - Implement `session-start`, `stop` handlers\n   - JSON input parsing for OpenCode event format\n\n2. **OpenCode Plugin: Basic Events**\n   - Subscribe to `session.created`, `session.idle`\n   - Spawn Entire CLI commands\n   - Export transcript on demand\n\n3. **Session Data Export**\n   - Export OpenCode session transcript to file\n   - Extract session metadata (ID, directory, timestamps)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- OpenCode sessions appear in `entire logs`\n- Users can create checkpoints manually\n- Basic rewind support\n\n**Estimated Effort:** 2-3 weeks\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Task Tracking\n\n**Goal:** Track subagent spawns and link transcripts\n\n**Components:**\n\n1. **Entire CLI: Task Hook Commands**\n   - Implement `pre-task`, `post-task` handlers\n   - Link subagent transcripts to task metadata\n\n2. **OpenCode Plugin: Task Events**\n   - Subscribe to `tool.execute.before/after` for Task tool\n   - Extract agent IDs from tool responses\n   - Export subagent transcripts\n\n3. **Task Checkpoint Metadata**\n   - Store task-specific data in `.entire/metadata/<session>/tasks/<tool-use-id>/`\n   - Include agent type, description, and transcript path\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Subagent work tracked as separate checkpoints\n- `entire logs` shows task hierarchy\n- Rewind to before/after subagent execution\n\n**Estimated Effort:** 2 weeks\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Enhanced Metadata\n\n**Goal:** Rich checkpoint descriptions and metadata\n\n**Components:**\n\n1. **Entire CLI: Todo Hook Command**\n   - Implement `post-todo` handler\n   - Extract in-progress todo content for checkpoint messages\n\n2. **OpenCode Plugin: Todo Events**\n   - Subscribe to `tool.execute.after` for TodoWrite tool\n   - Pass todo data to Entire CLI\n\n3. **User Prompt Tracking**\n   - Subscribe to `message.updated` events\n   - Detect user messages\n   - Implement `user-prompt-submit` handler\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Checkpoint messages reflect current task\n- User prompts captured in metadata\n- Better context for rewind points\n\n**Estimated Effort:** 1-2 weeks\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Polish & Production Ready\n\n**Goal:** Production-quality plugin with documentation\n\n**Components:**\n\n1. **Error Handling**\n   - Retry logic for transient failures\n   - Graceful degradation if Entire CLI not available\n   - User-friendly error messages\n\n2. **Performance Optimization**\n   - Hook debouncing for rapid events\n   - Batch checkpoint updates\n   - Async command execution\n\n3. **Documentation**\n   - Installation guide\n   - Configuration options\n   - Troubleshooting guide\n   - Architecture diagrams\n\n4. **Testing**\n   - Unit tests for plugin hooks\n   - Integration tests with Entire CLI\n   - Multi-agent scenario tests\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- NPM package published\n- Comprehensive documentation\n- CI/CD pipeline for plugin\n- Performance benchmarks\n\n**Estimated Effort:** 2-3 weeks\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Component Design\n\n### 1. Entire CLI: OpenCode Hook Commands\n\n#### File Structure\n```\ncmd/entire/cli/\n├── hooks_opencode_cmd.go        # Cobra command: entire hooks opencode\n├── hooks_opencode_handlers.go   # Hook handler functions\n├── agent/opencode/\n│   ├── opencode.go              # OpenCodeAgent implementation\n│   ├── types.go                 # OpenCode-specific types\n│   ├── session.go               # Session discovery\n│   └── hooks.go                 # HookHandler implementation\n```\n\n#### Command Structure\n```go\n// hooks_opencode_cmd.go\nvar hooksOpencodeCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"opencode\",\n    Short: \"OpenCode agent hooks\",\n}\n\nvar sessionStartCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"session-start\",\n    Short: \"Initialize OpenCode session tracking\",\n    RunE:  handleOpencodeSessionStart,\n}\n\nvar stopCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"stop\",\n    Short: \"Save checkpoint when OpenCode session ends\",\n    RunE:  handleOpencodeStop,\n}\n\nvar preTaskCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"pre-task\",\n    Short: \"Create checkpoint before Task tool execution\",\n    RunE:  handleOpencodePreTask,\n}\n\nvar postTaskCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"post-task\",\n    Short: \"Link subagent transcript after Task tool execution\",\n    RunE:  handleOpencodePostTask,\n}\n\nvar postTodoCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"post-todo\",\n    Short: \"Update checkpoint with todo metadata\",\n    RunE:  handleOpencodePostTodo,\n}\n```\n\n#### Input Format\n```go\n// OpenCodeHookInput represents JSON from OpenCode plugin\ntype OpenCodeHookInput struct {\n    SessionID      string          `json:\"session_id\"`\n    SessionRef     string          `json:\"session_ref\"`\n    Timestamp      string          `json:\"timestamp\"`\n\n    // Tool-specific (for task hooks)\n    ToolName       string          `json:\"tool_name,omitempty\"`\n    ToolUseID      string          `json:\"tool_use_id,omitempty\"`\n    ToolInput      json.RawMessage `json:\"tool_input,omitempty\"`\n    ToolResponse   json.RawMessage `json:\"tool_response,omitempty\"`\n\n    // Transcript paths\n    TranscriptPath string          `json:\"transcript_path,omitempty\"`\n    SubagentTranscriptPath string  `json:\"subagent_transcript_path,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n#### Handler Implementation Example\n```go\n// hooks_opencode_handlers.go\nfunc handleOpencodeSessionStart(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    input, err := parseOpencodeHookInput(cmd.InOrStdin())\n    if err != nil {\n        return NewSilentError(fmt.Errorf(\"invalid input: %w\", err))\n    }\n\n    // Get the configured strategy\n    strat, err := strategy.GetConfiguredStrategy()\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    // Initialize session (similar to Claude Code session-start)\n    ctx := strategy.SaveContext{\n        SessionID:      input.SessionID,\n        TranscriptPath: input.TranscriptPath,\n        PromptPath:     \"\", // OpenCode doesn't separate prompts\n        ContextPath:    \"\", // OpenCode doesn't generate context.md\n        Message:        \"Session started\",\n        IncrementalType: \"\",\n    }\n\n    if err := strat.SaveChanges(ctx); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to save session start: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc handleOpencodeStop(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    input, err := parseOpencodeHookInput(cmd.InOrStdin())\n    if err != nil {\n        return NewSilentError(fmt.Errorf(\"invalid input: %w\", err))\n    }\n\n    strat, err := strategy.GetConfiguredStrategy()\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    ctx := strategy.SaveContext{\n        SessionID:      input.SessionID,\n        TranscriptPath: input.TranscriptPath,\n        Message:        \"Session stopped\",\n    }\n\n    if err := strat.SaveChanges(ctx); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to save session stop: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc handleOpencodePreTask(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    input, err := parseOpencodeHookInput(cmd.InOrStdin())\n    if err != nil {\n        return NewSilentError(fmt.Errorf(\"invalid input: %w\", err))\n    }\n\n    strat, err := strategy.GetConfiguredStrategy()\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    // Extract task description from tool input\n    agentType, description := ParseSubagentTypeAndDescription(input.ToolInput)\n\n    message := fmt.Sprintf(\"Starting %s task: %s\", agentType, description)\n\n    ctx := strategy.SaveContext{\n        SessionID:       input.SessionID,\n        TranscriptPath:  input.TranscriptPath,\n        Message:         message,\n        IncrementalType: strategy.IncrementalTypeTaskStart,\n        TaskMetadataDir: fmt.Sprintf(\".entire/metadata/%s/tasks/%s\",\n                                     input.SessionID, input.ToolUseID),\n    }\n\n    if err := strat.SaveChanges(ctx); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to save pre-task checkpoint: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc handleOpencodePostTask(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    input, err := parseOpencodeHookInput(cmd.InOrStdin())\n    if err != nil {\n        return NewSilentError(fmt.Errorf(\"invalid input: %w\", err))\n    }\n\n    strat, err := strategy.GetConfiguredStrategy()\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    // Save task checkpoint with subagent transcript\n    ctx := strategy.TaskCheckpointContext{\n        SessionID:              input.SessionID,\n        SessionTranscriptPath:  input.TranscriptPath,\n        ToolUseID:              input.ToolUseID,\n        SubagentTranscriptPath: input.SubagentTranscriptPath,\n    }\n\n    if err := strat.SaveTaskCheckpoint(ctx); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to save post-task checkpoint: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\n### 2. OpenCode Plugin: TypeScript Implementation\n\n#### File Structure\n```\nopencode-entire-integration/\n├── package.json\n├── tsconfig.json\n├── src/\n│   ├── index.ts                 # Main plugin export\n│   ├── hooks/\n│   │   ├── session.ts           # Session lifecycle hooks\n│   │   ├── task.ts              # Task tool hooks\n│   │   └── todo.ts              # Todo tool hooks\n│   ├── export/\n│   │   ├── transcript.ts        # Export session transcripts\n│   │   └── metadata.ts          # Extract session metadata\n│   ├── cli/\n│   │   └── entire.ts            # Wrapper for entire CLI commands\n│   └── types.ts                 # Type definitions\n├── tests/\n│   └── ...\n└── README.md\n```\n\n#### Main Plugin Entry Point\n```typescript\n// src/index.ts\nimport type { Plugin } from \"@opencode-ai/plugin\"\nimport { SessionHooks } from \"./hooks/session\"\nimport { TaskHooks } from \"./hooks/task\"\nimport { TodoHooks } from \"./hooks/todo\"\n\nexport const EntireIntegrationPlugin: Plugin = async (ctx) => {\n  const { client, project, directory, worktree, $ } = ctx\n\n  // Initialize session hooks\n  const sessionHooks = SessionHooks({ client, project, directory, worktree, $ })\n  const taskHooks = TaskHooks({ client, project, directory, worktree, $ })\n  const todoHooks = TodoHooks({ client, project, directory, worktree, $ })\n\n  return {\n    // Session lifecycle\n    \"session.created\": sessionHooks.onSessionCreated,\n    \"session.idle\": sessionHooks.onSessionIdle,\n    \"session.status\": sessionHooks.onSessionStatus,\n\n    // Tool execution\n    \"tool.execute.before\": async (input, output) => {\n      if (input.tool === \"task\") {\n        await taskHooks.onPreTask(input, output)\n      }\n    },\n\n    \"tool.execute.after\": async (input, output) => {\n      if (input.tool === \"task\") {\n        await taskHooks.onPostTask(input, output)\n      } else if (input.tool === \"todo\") {\n        await todoHooks.onPostTodo(input, output)\n      }\n    },\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Session Hooks Implementation\n```typescript\n// src/hooks/session.ts\nimport type { Plugin, PluginInput } from \"@opencode-ai/plugin\"\nimport { exportTranscript } from \"../export/transcript\"\nimport { callEntireHook } from \"../cli/entire\"\n\nexport function SessionHooks({ client, project, directory, worktree, $ }: PluginInput) {\n  return {\n    async onSessionCreated({ event }: { event: any }) {\n      const sessionID = event.properties.info.id\n\n      try {\n        // Export transcript to file\n        const transcriptPath = await exportTranscript(sessionID, client)\n\n        // Call entire hooks opencode session-start\n        await callEntireHook($, \"session-start\", {\n          session_id: sessionID,\n          session_ref: sessionID,\n          timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n          transcript_path: transcriptPath,\n        })\n\n        await client.app.log({\n          service: \"entire-integration\",\n          level: \"info\",\n          message: \"Session tracking initialized\",\n          extra: { sessionID },\n        })\n      } catch (error) {\n        await client.app.log({\n          service: \"entire-integration\",\n          level: \"error\",\n          message: \"Failed to initialize session tracking\",\n          extra: { sessionID, error: String(error) },\n        })\n      }\n    },\n\n    async onSessionIdle({ event }: { event: any }) {\n      const sessionID = event.properties.sessionID\n\n      try {\n        const transcriptPath = await exportTranscript(sessionID, client)\n\n        await callEntireHook($, \"stop\", {\n          session_id: sessionID,\n          session_ref: sessionID,\n          timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n          transcript_path: transcriptPath,\n        })\n\n        await client.app.log({\n          service: \"entire-integration\",\n          level: \"info\",\n          message: \"Session checkpoint saved\",\n          extra: { sessionID },\n        })\n      } catch (error) {\n        await client.app.log({\n          service: \"entire-integration\",\n          level: \"warn\",\n          message: \"Failed to save session checkpoint\",\n          extra: { sessionID, error: String(error) },\n        })\n      }\n    },\n\n    async onSessionStatus({ event }: { event: any }) {\n      // Optional: save checkpoint on status change\n      // Can debounce to avoid too frequent saves\n    },\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Task Hooks Implementation\n```typescript\n// src/hooks/task.ts\nimport type { PluginInput } from \"@opencode-ai/plugin\"\nimport { exportTranscript } from \"../export/transcript\"\nimport { callEntireHook } from \"../cli/entire\"\n\nexport function TaskHooks({ client, project, directory, worktree, $ }: PluginInput) {\n  return {\n    async onPreTask(\n      input: { tool: string; sessionID: string; callID: string },\n      output: { args: any }\n    ) {\n      try {\n        const transcriptPath = await exportTranscript(input.sessionID, client)\n\n        await callEntireHook($, \"pre-task\", {\n          session_id: input.sessionID,\n          session_ref: input.sessionID,\n          timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n          tool_name: \"task\",\n          tool_use_id: input.callID,\n          tool_input: output.args,\n          transcript_path: transcriptPath,\n        })\n\n        await client.app.log({\n          service: \"entire-integration\",\n          level: \"debug\",\n          message: \"Pre-task checkpoint created\",\n          extra: {\n            sessionID: input.sessionID,\n            callID: input.callID,\n            agent: output.args.subagent_type,\n          },\n        })\n      } catch (error) {\n        await client.app.log({\n          service: \"entire-integration\",\n          level: \"error\",\n          message: \"Failed to create pre-task checkpoint\",\n          extra: { sessionID: input.sessionID, error: String(error) },\n        })\n      }\n    },\n\n    async onPostTask(\n      input: { tool: string; sessionID: string; callID: string },\n      output: { title: string; output: string; metadata: any }\n    ) {\n      try {\n        const transcriptPath = await exportTranscript(input.sessionID, client)\n\n        // Extract agent ID from metadata\n        const agentID = output.metadata?.agentId || \"\"\n\n        // Export subagent transcript if available\n        let subagentTranscriptPath = \"\"\n        if (agentID) {\n          subagentTranscriptPath = await exportTranscript(agentID, client)\n        }\n\n        await callEntireHook($, \"post-task\", {\n          session_id: input.sessionID,\n          session_ref: input.sessionID,\n          timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),\n          tool_name: \"task\",\n          tool_use_id: input.callID,\n          tool_response: { agentId: agentID },\n          transcript_path: transcriptPath,\n          subagent_transcript_path: subagentTranscriptPath,\n        })\n\n        await client.app.log({\n          service: \"entire-integration\",\n          level: \"debug\",\n          message: \"Post-task checkpoint created\",\n          extra: {\n            sessionID: input.sessionID,\n            callID: input.callID,\n            agentID,\n          },\n        })\n      } catch (error) {\n        await client.app.log({\n          service: \"entire-integration\",\n          level: \"error\",\n          message: \"Failed to create post-task checkpoint\",\n          extra: { sessionID: input.sessionID, error: String(error) },\n        })\n      }\n    },\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Entire CLI Wrapper\n```typescript\n// src/cli/entire.ts\nimport type { BunShell } from \"@opencode-ai/plugin\"\n\nexport async function callEntireHook(\n  $: BunShell,\n  hookName: string,\n  input: Record<string, any>\n): Promise<void> {\n  const inputJSON = JSON.stringify(input)\n\n  // Check if entire CLI is available\n  const checkResult = await $`which entire`.quiet().nothrow()\n  if (checkResult.exitCode !== 0) {\n    throw new Error(\"entire CLI not found in PATH. Please install entire CLI.\")\n  }\n\n  // Call entire hooks opencode <hook-name> with JSON input\n  const result = await $`entire hooks opencode ${hookName}`\n    .stdin(\"json\", input)\n    .quiet()\n    .nothrow()\n\n  if (result.exitCode !== 0) {\n    throw new Error(\n      `entire hooks opencode ${hookName} failed: ${result.stderr.toString()}`\n    )\n  }\n}\n```\n\n#### Transcript Export\n```typescript\n// src/export/transcript.ts\nimport type { ReturnType } from \"@opencode-ai/plugin\"\nimport path from \"path\"\nimport fs from \"fs/promises\"\n\ntype Client = ReturnType<typeof createOpencodeClient>\n\nexport async function exportTranscript(\n  sessionID: string,\n  client: Client\n): Promise<string> {\n  // Determine export path\n  const exportDir = path.join(\".entire\", \"opencode-sessions\", sessionID)\n  await fs.mkdir(exportDir, { recursive: true })\n\n  const transcriptPath = path.join(exportDir, \"transcript.jsonl\")\n\n  // Fetch session messages from OpenCode\n  const messages = await client.message.list({ sessionID })\n\n  // Convert to JSONL format\n  const lines = messages.data.map((msg) => JSON.stringify(msg))\n  const content = lines.join(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\"\n\n  // Write to file\n  await fs.writeFile(transcriptPath, content, \"utf-8\")\n\n  return transcriptPath\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Configuration & Setup\n\n### User Installation Steps\n\n1. **Install Entire CLI:**\n   ```bash\n   # Install entire CLI (if not already installed)\n   go install entire.io/cli/cmd/entire@latest\n\n   # Setup in repository\n   cd /path/to/project\n   entire setup --strategy=manual-commit\n   ```\n\n2. **Install OpenCode Plugin:**\n   ```bash\n   # Add plugin to OpenCode config\n   cat >> opencode.json << EOF\n   {\n     \"plugin\": [\"opencode-entire-integration\"]\n   }\n   EOF\n   ```\n\n3. **Verify Integration:**\n   ```bash\n   # Start OpenCode session\n   opencode\n\n   # In another terminal, check session tracking\n   entire logs\n   ```\n\n### Plugin Configuration Options\n\nThe plugin can accept configuration via `opencode.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"plugin\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"opencode-entire-integration\",\n      \"config\": {\n        \"enableTaskTracking\": true,\n        \"enableTodoTracking\": true,\n        \"exportTranscripts\": true,\n        \"logLevel\": \"info\",\n        \"debounceMs\": 500\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests (Plugin)\n\n```typescript\n// tests/hooks/session.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, mock } from \"bun:test\"\nimport { SessionHooks } from \"../src/hooks/session\"\n\ndescribe(\"SessionHooks\", () => {\n  it(\"should call entire CLI on session created\", async () => {\n    const mockClient = createMockClient()\n    const mock$ = createMock$()\n\n    const hooks = SessionHooks({\n      client: mockClient,\n      $: mock$,\n      // ... other context\n    })\n\n    await hooks.onSessionCreated({\n      event: {\n        properties: {\n          info: { id: \"test-session-123\" }\n        }\n      }\n    })\n\n    expect(mock$.called).toBe(true)\n    expect(mock$.args).toContain(\"session-start\")\n  })\n})\n```\n\n### Integration Tests (Entire CLI + Plugin)\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/opencode_test.go\n//go:build integration\n\nfunc TestOpenCodeSessionTracking(t *testing.T) {\n    env := setupTestEnv(t)\n    defer env.Cleanup()\n\n    // Setup entire CLI with manual-commit strategy\n    setupEntire(t, env.RepoDir, \"manual-commit\")\n\n    // Simulate OpenCode session-start hook\n    input := OpencodeHookInput{\n        SessionID:      \"test-session-001\",\n        SessionRef:     \"test-session-001\",\n        Timestamp:      time.Now().Format(time.RFC3339),\n        TranscriptPath: createTestTranscript(t, env.RepoDir),\n    }\n\n    cmd := exec.Command(\"entire\", \"hooks\", \"opencode\", \"session-start\")\n    cmd.Dir = env.RepoDir\n    cmd.Stdin = jsonInput(t, input)\n\n    output, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n    require.NoError(t, err, string(output))\n\n    // Verify session appears in logs\n    logs := runEntireLogs(t, env.RepoDir)\n    require.Contains(t, logs, \"test-session-001\")\n}\n\nfunc TestOpenCodeTaskTracking(t *testing.T) {\n    env := setupTestEnv(t)\n    defer env.Cleanup()\n\n    setupEntire(t, env.RepoDir, \"manual-commit\")\n\n    // Session start\n    sessionID := \"test-session-002\"\n    startSession(t, env.RepoDir, sessionID)\n\n    // Pre-task hook\n    toolUseID := \"task-001\"\n    preTaskInput := OpencodeHookInput{\n        SessionID:  sessionID,\n        SessionRef: sessionID,\n        ToolName:   \"task\",\n        ToolUseID:  toolUseID,\n        ToolInput:  json.RawMessage(`{\"subagent_type\":\"general-purpose\",\"description\":\"test task\"}`),\n        TranscriptPath: createTestTranscript(t, env.RepoDir),\n    }\n\n    runOpencodeHook(t, env.RepoDir, \"pre-task\", preTaskInput)\n\n    // Post-task hook\n    postTaskInput := OpencodeHookInput{\n        SessionID:  sessionID,\n        SessionRef: sessionID,\n        ToolName:   \"task\",\n        ToolUseID:  toolUseID,\n        ToolResponse: json.RawMessage(`{\"agentId\":\"agent-123\"}`),\n        TranscriptPath: createTestTranscript(t, env.RepoDir),\n        SubagentTranscriptPath: createTestTranscript(t, env.RepoDir),\n    }\n\n    runOpencodeHook(t, env.RepoDir, \"post-task\", postTaskInput)\n\n    // Verify task checkpoint exists\n    logs := runEntireLogs(t, env.RepoDir)\n    require.Contains(t, logs, \"test task\")\n    require.Contains(t, logs, toolUseID)\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Deployment & Distribution\n\n### NPM Package\n\n```json\n// package.json\n{\n  \"name\": \"opencode-entire-integration\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"description\": \"OpenCode plugin for Entire CLI session tracking\",\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"types\": \"dist/index.d.ts\",\n  \"keywords\": [\"opencode\", \"plugin\", \"entire\", \"git\", \"session-tracking\"],\n  \"author\": \"Entire Team\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\":