\n**Rationale:**\n- Clear identification in logs and commands\n- Allows OpenCode-specific session discovery logic\n- Consistent with existing \"ClaudeCode\" agent type\n- Enables future OpenCode-specific features\n\n**Implementation:**\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/agent/opencode/opencode.go\ntype OpenCodeAgent struct{}\n\nfunc (o *OpenCodeAgent) Name() string {\n    return \"OpenCode\"\n}\n\nfunc (o *OpenCodeAgent) Detect() bool {\n    // Check for .opencode/ directory or opencode.json\n    _, err1 := os.Stat(\".opencode\")\n    _, err2 := os.Stat(\"opencode.json\")\n    return err1 == nil || err2 == nil\n}\n```\n\nCommands:\n- `entire hooks opencode <hook-name>`\n- `entire opencode setup` (installs plugin)\n- `entire opencode status` (checks integration)\n\n---\n\n### 4. Configuration Location\n**Decision:** `.entire/opencode/` directory\n\n**Rationale:**\n- Keeps OpenCode-specific config separate from core Entire settings\n- Allows storing plugin state, exported transcripts, temp files\n- Clear namespace for OpenCode integration\n\n**Directory Structure:**\n```\n.entire/\n├── settings.json           # Core Entire settings (strategy, etc.)\n├── metadata/               # Session metadata (all agents)\n│   └── <session-id>/\n│       └── full.jsonl\n└── opencode/              # OpenCode-specific\n    ├── config.json         # Plugin configuration\n    ├── sessions/           # Exported session data\n    │   └── <session-id>/\n    │       ├── transcript.jsonl\n    │       └── metadata.json\n    └── plugin-version.txt  # Track installed plugin version\n```\n\n**Configuration Options:**\n```json\n// .entire/opencode/config.json\n{\n  \"enable_task_tracking\": true,\n  \"enable_todo_tracking\": true,\n  \"export_transcripts\": true,\n  \"hook_timeout_ms\": 5000,\n  \"log_level\": \"info\",\n  \"debounce_ms\": 500\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Error Handling & Installation\n\n**Decision:** Hybrid approach - both tools check for each other, surface clear errors, provide installation paths\n\n#### Option A: Plugin checks for Entire CLI\n\n**When:** Plugin initializes (OpenCode startup)\n\n**Behavior:**\n```typescript\n// Plugin initialization\nasync function checkEntireCLI($: BunShell): Promise<boolean> {\n  const result = await $`which entire`.quiet().nothrow()\n\n  if (result.exitCode !== 0) {\n    console.error(\"╭─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\")\n    console.error(\"│  ⚠️  Entire CLI not found                       │\")\n    console.error(\"│                                                 │\")\n    console.error(\"│  Install with:                                  │\")\n    console.error(\"│    go install entire.io/cli/cmd/entire@latest   │\")\n    console.error(\"│                                                 │\")\n    console.error(\"│  Or visit: https://entire.io/cli                │\")\n    console.error(\"╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\")\n    return false\n  }\n\n  return true\n}\n\nexport const EntireIntegrationPlugin: Plugin = async (ctx) => {\n  const hasEntire = await checkEntireCLI(ctx.$)\n\n  if (!hasEntire) {\n    // Plugin loads but does nothing\n    // User sees error on every OpenCode startup until they install\n    return {}\n  }\n\n  // Normal plugin initialization\n  return {\n    \"session.created\": /* ... */,\n    // ... other hooks\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**User Experience:**\n1. User installs plugin: `npm install opencode-entire-integration`\n2. User adds to `opencode.json`: `\"plugin\": [\"opencode-entire-integration\"]`\n3. User starts OpenCode\n4. Plugin prints error if Entire CLI missing\n5. User installs Entire CLI\n6. Plugin works on next OpenCode startup\n\n#### Option B: Entire CLI installs plugin\n\n**Command:** `entire opencode setup`\n\n**Behavior:**\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/opencode_setup_cmd.go\nfunc runOpencodeSetup(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    // 1. Check if OpenCode is installed\n    if !isOpencodeInstalled() {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"OpenCode not found. Install from: https://opencode.ai\")\n    }\n\n    // 2. Check if plugin already installed\n    if isPluginInstalled() {\n        fmt.Println(\"✓ Plugin already installed\")\n        return nil\n    }\n\n    // 3. Install plugin via Bun\n    fmt.Println(\"Installing opencode-entire-integration plugin...\")\n\n    // Find OpenCode config location\n    configPath := findOpencodeConfig()\n\n    // Install via Bun to the appropriate location\n    cmd := exec.Command(\"bun\", \"add\", \"opencode-entire-integration\")\n    cmd.Dir = filepath.Dir(configPath)\n\n    if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to install plugin: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    // 4. Add to opencode.json\n    if err := addPluginToConfig(configPath); err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    fmt.Println(\"✓ OpenCode integration configured\")\n    fmt.Println(\"  Entire CLI will now track OpenCode sessions\")\n\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc findOpencodeConfig() string {\n    // Try project config first\n    if _, err := os.Stat(\"opencode.json\"); err == nil {\n        return \"opencode.json\"\n    }\n\n    // Fall back to global config\n    home, _ := os.UserHomeDir()\n    return filepath.Join(home, \".config\", \"opencode\", \"opencode.json\")\n}\n\nfunc addPluginToConfig(configPath string) error {\n    // Read existing config\n    data, err := os.ReadFile(configPath)\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    var config map[string]interface{}\n    json.Unmarshal(data, &config)\n\n    // Add plugin if not present\n    plugins, _ := config[\"plugin\"].([]interface{})\n\n    pluginExists := false\n    for _, p := range plugins {\n        if p == \"opencode-entire-integration\" {\n            pluginExists = true\n            break\n        }\n    }\n\n    if !pluginExists {\n        plugins = append(plugins, \"opencode-entire-integration\")\n        config[\"plugin\"] = plugins\n    }\n\n    // Write back\n    output, _ := json.MarshalIndent(config, \"\", \"  \")\n    return os.WriteFile(configPath, output, 0o644)\n}\n```\n\n**User Experience:**\n1. User has OpenCode installed\n2. User runs `entire setup` (normal setup)\n3. User runs `entire opencode setup`\n4. Entire CLI installs plugin automatically\n5. Everything works\n\n#### Option C: Bundle Entire CLI with plugin (NOT RECOMMENDED)\n\n**Why not:**\n- Platform-specific binaries (would need Linux/Mac/Windows builds)\n- Large package size\n- npm postinstall scripts are often blocked in corporate environments\n- Version management complexity (plugin version != CLI version)\n- Security concerns (downloading/executing binaries)\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Installation Flow\n\n### Approach: Hybrid with explicit setup command\n\n**For new users (never used Entire):**\n```bash\n# 1. Install Entire CLI\ngo install entire.io/cli/cmd/entire@latest\n\n# 2. Setup in repository\ncd /path/to/project\nentire setup\n\n# 3. Setup OpenCode integration\nentire opencode setup\n```\n\n**For existing Entire users:**\n```bash\n# Just run the OpenCode setup\nentire opencode setup\n```\n\n**For OpenCode users who manually install plugin:**\n```bash\n# Add to opencode.json\n{\n  \"plugin\": [\"opencode-entire-integration\"]\n}\n\n# Plugin will show error if Entire CLI missing\n# Follow instructions to install Entire CLI\n```\n\n### Benefits of this approach:\n\n1. **Clear error messages:** Plugin shows exactly what to install\n2. **Automatic setup:** `entire opencode setup` does everything\n3. **Flexible:** Works with manual plugin installation too\n4. **Version control:** Entire CLI controls plugin version compatibility\n5. **User-friendly:** Single command to set up integration\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### Plugin Package Metadata\n\n```json\n// package.json for opencode-entire-integration\n{\n  \"name\": \"opencode-entire-integration\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"description\": \"OpenCode plugin for Entire CLI session tracking\",\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"opencode-entire-check\": \"./bin/check-setup.js\"\n  },\n  \"peerDependencies\": {\n    \"@opencode-ai/plugin\": \"^0.1.0\"\n  },\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"bun\": \">=1.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Setup Command Implementation\n\n```go\n// cmd/entire/cli/opencode_setup_cmd.go\n\nvar opencodeCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"opencode\",\n    Short: \"OpenCode integration commands\",\n}\n\nvar opencodeSetupCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"setup\",\n    Short: \"Setup OpenCode integration (installs plugin)\",\n    Long: `Installs and configures the opencode-entire-integration plugin.\n\nThis will:\n  1. Check if OpenCode is installed\n  2. Install the opencode-entire-integration plugin\n  3. Add the plugin to your OpenCode configuration\n  4. Create .entire/opencode/ directory for configuration\n\nAfter setup, OpenCode sessions will be automatically tracked by Entire CLI.`,\n    RunE: runOpencodeSetup,\n}\n\nvar opencodeStatusCmd = &cobra.Command{\n    Use:   \"status\",\n    Short: \"Check OpenCode integration status\",\n    RunE:  runOpencodeStatus,\n}\n\nfunc init() {\n    opencodeCmd.AddCommand(opencodeSetupCmd)\n    opencodeCmd.AddCommand(opencodeStatusCmd)\n    rootCmd.AddCommand(opencodeCmd)\n}\n\nfunc runOpencodeSetup(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    fmt.Println(\"Setting up OpenCode integration...\")\n\n    // 1. Check prerequisites\n    if err := checkPrerequisites(); err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    // 2. Create .entire/opencode directory\n    if err := os.MkdirAll(\".entire/opencode\", 0o755); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to create .entire/opencode: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    // 3. Install plugin\n    if err := installPlugin(); err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    // 4. Create default config\n    if err := createDefaultConfig(); err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    // 5. Verify installation\n    if err := verifySetup(); err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    fmt.Println()\n    fmt.Println(\"✓ OpenCode integration configured successfully!\")\n    fmt.Println()\n    fmt.Println(\"Next steps:\")\n    fmt.Println(\"  1. Start OpenCode: opencode\")\n    fmt.Println(\"  2. Sessions will be tracked automatically\")\n    fmt.Println(\"  3. View sessions: entire logs\")\n    fmt.Println(\"  4. Rewind: entire rewind\")\n\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc checkPrerequisites() error {\n    // Check for OpenCode\n    cmd := exec.Command(\"which\", \"opencode\")\n    if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"OpenCode not found. Install from: https://opencode.ai\")\n    }\n\n    // Check for Bun (needed to install plugin)\n    cmd = exec.Command(\"which\", \"bun\")\n    if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"Bun not found. Install from: https://bun.sh\")\n    }\n\n    // Check for git repository\n    if _, err := paths.RepoRoot(); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"not a git repository. Run from a git repository root\")\n    }\n\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc installPlugin() error {\n    fmt.Println(\"Installing opencode-entire-integration plugin...\")\n\n    // Determine config location (project vs global)\n    var configDir string\n    if _, err := os.Stat(\"opencode.json\"); err == nil {\n        configDir = \".\"\n    } else {\n        home, _ := os.UserHomeDir()\n        configDir = filepath.Join(home, \".config\", \"opencode\")\n        os.MkdirAll(configDir, 0o755)\n    }\n\n    // Install via Bun\n    cmd := exec.Command(\"bun\", \"add\", \"opencode-entire-integration\")\n    cmd.Dir = configDir\n    cmd.Stdout = os.Stdout\n    cmd.Stderr = os.Stderr\n\n    if err := cmd.Run(); err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"failed to install plugin: %w\", err)\n    }\n\n    // Update opencode.json\n    configPath := filepath.Join(configDir, \"opencode.json\")\n    if err := addPluginToConfig(configPath); err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n\n    // Record installed version\n    if err := recordPluginVersion(); err != nil {\n        // Non-fatal\n        fmt.Printf(\"Warning: failed to record plugin version: %v\\n\", err)\n    }\n\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc createDefaultConfig() error {\n    configPath := \".entire/opencode/config.json\"\n\n    // Skip if exists\n    if _, err := os.Stat(configPath); err == nil {\n        return nil\n    }\n\n    defaultConfig := map[string]interface{}{\n        \"enable_task_tracking\": true,\n        \"enable_todo_tracking\": true,\n        \"export_transcripts\":   true,\n        \"hook_timeout_ms\":      5000,\n        \"log_level\":           \"info\",\n        \"debounce_ms\":         500,\n    }\n\n    data, _ := json.MarshalIndent(defaultConfig, \"\", \"  \")\n    return os.WriteFile(configPath, data, 0o644)\n}\n\nfunc verifySetup() error {\n    // Check plugin is in opencode.json\n    // Check .entire/opencode exists\n    // Try running opencode --version\n    return nil\n}\n\nfunc runOpencodeStatus(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {\n    fmt.Println(\"OpenCode Integration Status\")\n    fmt.Println(\"=\" + strings.Repeat(\"=\", 30))\n\n    // Check OpenCode installed\n    if err := exec.Command(\"which\", \"opencode\").Run(); err != nil {\n        fmt.Println(\"✗ OpenCode: Not installed\")\n    } else {\n        fmt.Println(\"✓ OpenCode: Installed\")\n    }\n\n    // Check plugin installed\n    pluginInstalled := isPluginInstalled()\n    if pluginInstalled {\n        version := getPluginVersion()\n        fmt.Printf(\"✓ Plugin: Installed (v%s)\\n\", version)\n    } else {\n        fmt.Println(\"✗ Plugin: Not installed\")\n        fmt.Println(\"  Run: entire opencode setup\")\n    }\n\n    // Check config exists\n    if _, err := os.Stat(\".entire/opencode/config.json\"); err == nil {\n        fmt.Println(\"✓ Config: Found\")\n    } else {\n        fmt.Println(\"✗ Config: Not found\")\n    }\n\n    // Check for recent sessions\n    sessions := findOpencodeSessionsInLogs()\n    fmt.Printf(\"  Sessions tracked: %d\\n\", len(sessions))\n\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\n### Plugin Error Handling\n\n```typescript\n// src/index.ts - Plugin entry point with error surfacing\n\nexport const EntireIntegrationPlugin: Plugin = async (ctx) => {\n  const { $, client, directory } = ctx\n\n  // Check for Entire CLI on initialization\n  const hasEntire = await checkEntireCLI($)\n\n  if (!hasEntire) {\n    // Log to OpenCode's logging system\n    await client.app.log({\n      service: \"entire-integration\",\n      level: \"error\",\n      message: \"Entire CLI not found. Session tracking disabled.\",\n      extra: {\n        installUrl: \"https://entire.io/cli\",\n        installCommand: \"go install entire.io/cli/cmd/entire@latest\",\n      }\n    })\n\n    // Return empty hooks (plugin loads but does nothing)\n    return {}\n  }\n\n  // Check if entire setup has been run\n  const isSetup = await checkEntireSetup(directory)\n\n  if (!isSetup) {\n    await client.app.log({\n      service: \"entire-integration\",\n      level: \"warn\",\n      message: \"Entire CLI not configured in this repository\",\n      extra: {\n        setupCommand: \"cd \" + directory + \" && entire setup\",\n      }\n    })\n\n    // Still return empty hooks\n    return {}\n  }\n\n  // Everything OK, return actual hooks\n  await client.app.log({\n    service: \"entire-integration\",\n    level: \"info\",\n    message: \"Entire CLI integration active\",\n    extra: { directory }\n  })\n\n  return {\n    \"session.created\": /* ... */,\n    \"tool.execute.before\": /* ... */,\n    // ... other hooks\n  }\n}\n\nasync function checkEntireCLI($: BunShell): Promise<boolean> {\n  const result = await $`which entire`.quiet().nothrow()\n  return result.exitCode === 0\n}\n\nasync function checkEntireSetup(directory: string): Promise<boolean> {\n  // Check for .entire/settings.json\n  try {\n    const settingsPath = path.join(directory, \".entire\", \"settings.json\")\n    await fs.access(settingsPath)\n    return true\n  } catch {\n    return false\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## User Journeys\n\n### Journey 1: New to both Entire and OpenCode\n\n```bash\n# Install tools\ngo install entire.io/cli/cmd/entire@latest\nbrew install opencode  # or equivalent\n\n# Setup\ncd my-project\ngit init\nentire setup\nentire opencode setup\n\n# Use\nopencode\n# ... work with AI ...\nentire logs\nentire rewind\n```\n\n### Journey 2: Existing Entire user, new to OpenCode\n\n```bash\n# Already has Entire CLI\ncd my-project\n\n# Install OpenCode\nbrew install opencode\n\n# Setup integration\nentire opencode setup\n\n# Use\nopencode\n# Sessions automatically tracked\n```\n\n### Journey 3: Existing OpenCode user, new to Entire\n\n```bash\n# Already uses OpenCode\ncd my-project\n\n# Install Entire\ngo install entire.io/cli/cmd/entire@latest\nentire setup\n\n# Setup integration\nentire opencode setup\n\n# Use\nopencode\n# Sessions now tracked\nentire logs\n```\n\n### Journey 4: Manual plugin installation\n\n```bash\n# User installs plugin manually\ncd ~/.config/opencode\nbun add opencode-entire-integration\n\n# Edit opencode.json\n{\n  \"plugin\": [\"opencode-entire-integration\"]\n}\n\n# Start OpenCode\nopencode\n\n# Plugin shows error if Entire CLI missing\n# ╭─────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n# │  ⚠️  Entire CLI not found                       │\n# │  Install: go install entire.io/cli/cmd/entire@latest │\n# ╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n# User installs Entire CLI\ngo install entire.io/cli/cmd/entire@latest\ncd my-project\nentire setup\n\n# Plugin works on next OpenCode startup\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n**Installation Strategy:** Hybrid approach with `entire opencode setup` command\n\n**Key Benefits:**\n1. ✓ Clear error messages when dependencies missing\n2. ✓ Automatic plugin installation via Entire CLI\n3. ✓ Manual installation also supported\n4. ✓ Version compatibility managed by Entire CLI\n5. ✓ User-friendly single command setup\n\n**Next Steps:**\n1. Implement `entire opencode setup` and `entire opencode status` commands\n2. Implement plugin with proper error surfacing\n3. Test all user journeys\n4. Document in README with examples\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"532c9964-dd9e-4d3c-9d6f-a00226491c95"}
