 for transcript export\n```\n\n### 5. Submit Pull Request\n\n- Push your branch to GitHub\n- Create a pull request with a clear description\n- Link any related issues\n- Wait for CI checks to pass\n- Address review feedback\n\n## Code Style\n\n### TypeScript\n\n- Use explicit types where helpful for clarity\n- Avoid `any` (use `unknown` if type is truly unknown)\n- Use async/await over promises\n- Prefer functional patterns over imperative\n\n**Good:**\n```typescript\nasync function exportTranscript(\n  sessionID: string,\n  client: Client,\n  directory: string\n): Promise<ExportedTranscript> {\n  // Implementation\n}\n```\n\n**Bad:**\n```typescript\nfunction exportTranscript(sessionID: any, client: any, directory: any): any {\n  // Implementation\n}\n```\n\n### Error Handling\n\n- Always handle errors gracefully\n- Provide helpful error messages\n- Log errors with context\n- Don't expose internal details to users\n\n**Good:**\n```typescript\ntry {\n  await entireCLI.callHook(\"session-start\", input)\n} catch (error) {\n  await logger.error(\"Failed to initialize session tracking\", {\n    sessionID,\n    error: String(error),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Testing\n\n- Write tests for all public APIs\n- Test happy path and error cases\n- Use descriptive test names\n- Mock external dependencies\n\n**Good:**\n```typescript\ndescribe(\"EntireCLI\", () => {\n  describe(\"isInstalled\", () => {\n    it(\"should return true when entire CLI is in PATH\", async () => {\n      // Test implementation\n    })\n\n    it(\"should return false when entire CLI is not in PATH\", async () => {\n      // Test implementation\n    })\n  })\n})\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── index.ts                    # Main plugin entry point\n├── types.ts                    # TypeScript type definitions\n├── hooks/\n│   └── session.ts              # Session lifecycle hooks\n├── export/\n│   └── transcript.ts           # Transcript export logic\n├── cli/\n│   └── entire.ts               # Entire CLI wrapper\n└── utils/\n    ├── logger.ts               # Logging utilities\n    └── config.ts               # Configuration management\n\ntest/\n├── cli.test.ts                 # CLI wrapper tests\n├── config.test.ts              # Configuration tests\n└── transcript.test.ts          # Transcript export tests\n```\n\n## Testing\n\n### Unit Tests\n\nRun unit tests with Bun's test runner:\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests\nbun test\n\n# Run specific test file\nbun test test/cli.test.ts\n\n# Watch mode\nbun test --watch\n\n# Coverage\nbun test --coverage\n```\n\n### Integration Tests\n\nFor integration testing with real Entire CLI and OpenCode:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Build the plugin\nbun run build\n\n# 2. Link locally\ncd ~/.config/opencode\nbun link /path/to/opencode-entire-integration\n\n# 3. Add to opencode.json\n{\n  \"plugin\": [\"opencode-entire-integration\"]\n}\n\n# 4. Test with OpenCode\ncd /path/to/test/project\nentire setup\nopencode\n```\n\n### Manual Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] Plugin loads without errors\n- [ ] Session created triggers hook\n- [ ] Transcript exported correctly\n- [ ] Session appears in `entire logs`\n- [ ] Can rewind to session checkpoint\n- [ ] Error messages clear and helpful\n- [ ] Missing Entire CLI detected\n- [ ] Missing setup detected\n\n## Adding New Features\n\n### Phase 2: Task Tracking\n\nTo add task tracking hooks:\n\n1. Create `src/hooks/task.ts` with task hook implementations\n2. Add tests in `test/task.test.ts`\n3. Update `src/index.ts` to wire up hooks\n4. Update configuration to enable/disable\n5. Document in README\n\n### Phase 3: Todo Metadata\n\nTo add todo tracking:\n\n1. Create `src/hooks/todo.ts` with todo hook implementations\n2. Add extraction logic for todo content\n3. Add tests\n4. Wire up in main plugin\n5. Document\n\n## Performance Considerations\n\n- **Hook execution:** Keep hooks fast (< 100ms target)\n- **Transcript export:** Only export when needed\n- **Debouncing:** Use config.debounce_ms for rapid events\n- **Error handling:** Don't block OpenCode on failures\n\n## Debugging\n\n### Enable Debug Logging\n\n```json\n// .entire/opencode/config.json\n{\n  \"log_level\": \"debug\"\n}\n```\n\n### View OpenCode Logs\n\n```bash\nopencode --debug\n```\n\n### Check Entire CLI Status\n\n```bash\nentire logs\nentire rewind --dry-run\n```\n\n### Test Hook Manually\n\n```bash\necho '{\n  \"session_id\": \"test-123\",\n  \"session_ref\": \"test-123\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-01T00:00:00Z\"\n}' | entire hooks opencode session-start\n```\n\n## Release Process\n\n1. Update version in `package.json`\n2. Update `CHANGELOG.md`\n3. Create git tag: `git tag v0.1.0`\n4. Push tag: `git push origin v0.1.0`\n5. CI will build and publish to NPM\n\n## Questions?\n\n- Open an issue on GitHub\n- Check the [documentation](../cli/docs/README-opencode-integration.md)\n- Review existing code for patterns\n\n## License\n\nBy contributing, you agree that your contributions will be licensed under the MIT License.\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":90498,"cache_read_input_tokens":13734,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":90498,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CWyefT1QFhqxCQvGnEjqs","type":"assistant","uuid":"cffc025b-32c7-4f09-8bb3-a926a16636c3","timestamp":"2026-01-10T11:52:58.678Z"}
