{"parentUuid":"182118be-6ae4-468a-b9b8-52fb9bbd3809","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/opencode-entire-integration","sessionId":"52c38054-a209-4b88-9a0d-d98ba15865dd","version":"2.1.3","gitBranch":"soph/opencode","slug":"vectorized-weaving-quail","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SuA7vN9Mou778U5brT6aDJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenCode Plugin Events\n\nOpenCode emits various events that plugins can subscribe to. Here's the complete list organized by category:\n\n## Available Events\n\n**Command Events:**\n- `command.executed`\n\n**File Events:**\n- `file.edited`\n- `file.watcher.updated`\n\n**Installation Events:**\n- `installation.updated`\n\n**LSP Events:**\n- `lsp.client.diagnostics`\n- `lsp.updated`\n\n**Message Events:**\n- `message.part.removed`\n- `message.part.updated`\n- `message.removed`\n- `message.updated`\n\n**Permission Events:**\n- `permission.replied`\n- `permission.updated`\n\n**Server Events:**\n- `server.connected`\n\n**Session Events:**\n- `session.created`, `session.compacted`, `session.deleted`\n- `session.diff`, `session.error`, `session.idle`\n- `session.status`, `session.updated`\n\n**Todo Events:**\n- `todo.updated`\n\n**Tool Events:**\n- `tool.execute.after`\n- `tool.execute.before`\n\n**TUI Events:**\n- `tui.prompt.append`\n- `tui.command.execute`\n- `tui.toast.show`\n\n## Subscribing to Events\n\nTo subscribe to events, return a hooks object from your plugin function:\n\n```javascript\nexport const MyPlugin = async (ctx) => {\n  return {\n    \"session.idle\": async (event) => {\n      // Handle the event\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe documentation notes that \"plugins can subscribe to events\" by implementing them in the returned hooks object, with each event receiving relevant data when triggered."}]},"uuid":"a4ef32d9-bd3c-40b2-8b6a-0699df31e904","timestamp":"2026-01-10T19:12:50.746Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":92596,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","r