{"parentUuid":"bd062c08-a048-4824-8289-6b523a3b9bcd","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/opencode-entire-integration","sessionId":"52c38054-a209-4b88-9a0d-d98ba15865dd","version":"2.1.3","gitBranch":"soph/opencode","slug":"vectorized-weaving-quail","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LDguUa3jPy21GkKzHDEvQ1","type":"tool_result","content":"# Opencode Plugin Structure and Export Pattern\n\n## Complete Plugin Structure\n\nA plugin follows this export pattern:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Plugin, tool } from '@opencode-ai/plugin'\n\nexport const MyPlugin: Plugin = async (ctx) => {\n  return {\n    tool: { /* tool definitions */ },\n    auth: { /* auth config */ },\n    event: async ({ event }) => { /* handler */ },\n    config: async (config) => { /* modifications */ },\n    'chat.message': async ({}, { message }) => { /* hook */ },\n    // ... additional hooks\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Key Architectural Details\n\n**Asynchronous Plugin Loading:** The plugin function itself is `async` and returns hooks asynchronously. Per the documentation: *\"A plugin is a TypeScript module that exports a function conforming to the `Plugin` type\"* that operates as an async function.\n\n**Hook Return Pattern:** While the plugin factory function is async, individual hooks within the returned object are also async. For instance, the configuration hook signature shows: *\"config: async (config) => (config.myPlugin = { enabled: true })\"*\n\n## Context Parameter (ctx)\n\nThe plugin receives a context object providing:\n- `ctx.client` - Opencode SDK client\n- `ctx.project.id`, `.worktree`, `.vcs` - Project metadata\n- `ctx.$` - Bun shell for command execution\n- `ctx.directory` - Working directory\n\n## Hook Categories\n\nPlugins can define hooks for:\n- **Tools** - Custom AI-executable functions\n- **Authentication** - OAuth and API key providers\n- **Events** - System event handlers\n- **Chat/LLM** - Message and parameter modification\n- **Permissions** - Access control decisions\n- **Tool execution** - Pre/post-execution interception\n- **Configuration** - Setting modifications"}]},"uuid":"db425974-d041-43ee-8742-2f9ea44cf79a","timestamp":"2026-01-10T19:23:50.236Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":197473,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Opencode Plugin Structure and Export Pattern\n\n## Complete Plugin Structure\n\nA plugin follows this export pattern:\n\n```typescript\nimport { Plugin, tool } from '@opencode-ai/plugin'\n\nexport const MyPlugin: Plugin = async (ctx) => {\n  return {\n    tool: { /* tool definitions */ },\n    auth: { /* auth config */ },\n    event: async ({ event }) => { /* handler */ },\n    config: async (config) => { /* modifications */ },\n    'chat.message': async ({}, { message }) => { /* hook */ },\n    // ... additional hooks\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Key Architectural Details\n\n**Asynchronous Plugin Loading:** The plugin function itself is `async` and returns hooks asynchronously. Per the documentation: *\"A plugin is a TypeScript module that exports a function conforming to the `Plugin` type\"* that operates as an async function.\n\n**Hook Return Pattern:** While the plugin factory function is async, individual hooks within the returned object are also async. For instance, the configuration hook signature shows: *\"config: async (config) => (config.myPlugin = { enabled: true })\"*\n\n## Context Parameter (ctx)\n\nThe plugin receives a context object providing:\n- `ctx.client` - Opencode SDK client\n- `ctx.project.id`, `.worktree`, `.vcs` - Project metadata\n- `ctx.$` - Bun shell for command execution\n- `ctx.directory` - Working directory\n\n## Hook Categories\n\nPlugins can define hooks for:\n- **Tools** - Custom AI-executable functions\n- **Authentication** - OAuth and API key providers\n- **Events** - System event handlers\n- **Chat/LLM** - Message and parameter modification\n- **Permissions** - Access control decisions\n- **Tool execution** - Pre/post-execution interception\n- **Configuration** - Setting modifications","durationMs":8251,"url":"https://gist.github.com/rstacruz/946d02757525c9a0f49b25e316fbe715"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bd062c08-a048-4824-8289-6b523a3b9bcd"}
