ich is an async function implementing the Plugin interface.\n\n## Hook Architecture\n\nThe implementation provides two main hooks:\n\n**1. Auth Hook**\nThe plugin returns an `auth` object with a custom `loader` that wraps the fetch function. This loader intercepts all requests to inject Helicone tracking headers dynamically. The custom fetch adds `Helicone-Session-Id` and `Helicone-Session-Name` headers when available, respecting user-provided headers.\n\n**2. Event Hook**\nAn `event` handler processes session lifecycle events:\n- `\"session.created\"` – Captures new session data\n- `\"session.updated\"` – Updates existing session information\n\n## Key Utilities\n\n**sessionToUUID()** – Converts session IDs to deterministic UUID format using Bun's hash function\n\n**sanitizeForHeader()** – Strips control characters and whitespace to prevent HTTP header injection attacks\n\n## State Management\n\nGlobal variables (`currentSessionUUID`, `currentSessionName`) maintain session state accessible to the fetch wrapper, enabling consistent header injection across all outbound requests without modifying core provider code.","durationMs":3321,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/H2Shami/opencode-helicone-session/main/index.ts"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6c617ca6-c9f4-4298-b9d8-6ebfe38b2831"}
