{"parentUuid":"f13e4a7d-0391-48e7-a5f8-092150edfda2","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"52c38054-a209-4b88-9a0d-d98ba15865dd","version":"2.1.3","gitBranch":"soph/opencode","slug":"vectorized-weaving-quail","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01L8PCUMEZbgnee1yQtfEYpB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Great question! Here's why we have `.entire/opencode`:\n\n## Directory Structure Overview\n\n```\n.entire/\n├── settings.json              # Entire CLI settings (strategy, agent, etc.)\n├── logs/                      # Entire logs\n├── metadata/                  # ← CLI's PROCESSED metadata (used by git)\n│   └── 2026-01-10-<session>/\n│       ├── full.jsonl         # Copied from opencode\n│       ├── prompt.txt         # Extracted by CLI\n│       └── context.md         # Generated by CLI\n└── opencode/                  # ← OpenCode plugin's RAW exports\n    ├── config.json            # OpenCode plugin config (optional)\n    └── sessions/\n        └── ses_<id>/\n            ├── transcript.jsonl  # Raw OpenCode export\n            └── metadata.json     # OpenCode session metadata\n```\n\n## Why Two Separate Directories?\n\n### `.entire/opencode/` - Plugin's Raw Export Area\n\n**Purpose:** OpenCode plugin exports raw session data here\n- **Who writes:** OpenCode plugin (TypeScript)\n- **Format:** OpenCode's native JSONL format\n- **When:** Real-time during session (exported on session.created and session.idle events)\n- **Contains:** \n  - Raw transcript in OpenCode's format\n  - OpenCode's session metadata (title, timestamps, agent info)\n\n**Why separate?**\n- Keeps OpenCode's data isolated from CLI processing\n- OpenCode uses short session IDs: `ses_45655c115ffeAhIdsFfEtxjVhL`\n- Plugin can be configured via `.entire/opencode/config.json`\n\n### `.entire/metadata/` - CLI's Processed Metadata\n\n**Purpose:** Entire CLI's processed/transformed metadata\n- **Who writes:** Entire CLI (Go)\n- **Format:** Entire's standardized format\n- **When:** On stop hook (when session goes idle)\n- **Contains:**\n  - Copied transcript\n  - **Extracted** user prompts → `prompt.txt`\n  - **Generated** context summary → `context.md`\n  - File change tracking\n\n**Why separate?**\n- Uses Entire session IDs with date prefix: `2026-01-10-ses_45655c115ffeAhIdsFfEtxjVhL`\n- This is what gets committed to shadow branches and linked to git commits\n- Shared format with Claude Code for consistency\n\n## The Flow\n\n1. **OpenCode session happens** → Plugin exports to `.entire/opencode/sessions/ses_xxx/transcript.jsonl`\n2. **Session goes idle** → Plugin calls `entire hooks opencode stop`\n3. **CLI reads** from `.entire/opencode/sessions/ses_xxx/transcript.jsonl`\n4. **CLI processes**:\n   - Parses OpenCode's JSONL format\n   - Extracts prompts\n   - Detects file changes\n   - Generates context\n5. **CLI writes** to `.entire/metadata/2026-01-10-ses_xxx/`\n6. **CLI creates checkpoint** on shadow branch with link to metadata\n\n## Could We Use Just One Directory?\n\n**Technically yes**, but it would be messier:\n- Plugin and CLI would both write to same location\n- Session ID formats would be inconsistent\n- OpenCode-specific config would mix with Entire config\n- Harder to support multiple agents (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.)\n\nThe current design keeps concerns separated:\n- **`.entire/opencode/`** = \"OpenCode's data area\"\n- **`.entire/metadata/`** = \"Entire's standardized metadata\" (works for any agent)\n\nDoes this make sense? Would you prefer a different structure?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":302,"cache_read_input_tokens":131811,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":302,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":924,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CWzN7Sjn5bRYYqHKx5UeM","type":"assistant","uuid":"cacdbb7e-47a2-4d9a-8524-4c21e70b8dbc","ti